# USB gadget config: serial disabled, composite stack untouched.
#
# Both USB-serial architectures failed on this phone in ways that ate
# entire debug cycles (see SERIAL-BRIEF): the ACM+ECM configfs composite
# NAKed bulk-OUT forever, and legacy G_SERIAL brought a best-effort
# userspace (blocking opens, VT fights) that stalled boots and killed
# the greeter. So: no USB serial at all. G_SERIAL is off, nothing binds
# the UDC in normal boot, the host sees no USB device (U-Boot UMS and
# fastboot are bootloader-level and unaffected).
#
# The composite function stack stays builtin (=y, matching the pmOS
# pmaports reference config). The only thing ever assembled from it is
# the NCM *network* gadget (davinci-net-usb service + UDC hotplug rule,
# SERIAL-BRIEF §19): no ACM/serial function anywhere, no
# davinci_gadget serial hook, no ECM profile.
# Device access is panel getty (tty1) + USB-NCM/WiFi SSH + UMS pulls.
#
# Applied by scripts/build-kernel-local.sh via scripts/config
# (=y/--enable, =m/--module, =n/--disable), then olddefconfig.
# Physical UART (SERIAL_MSM / QCOM_GENI + consoles) stays builtin (=y,
# pmOS-verbatim) for test-point debugging; it is on no kernel cmdline.
CONFIG_USB_G_SERIAL=n
CONFIG_USB_LIBCOMPOSITE=y
CONFIG_USB_F_ACM=y
CONFIG_USB_F_SERIAL=y
CONFIG_USB_F_OBEX=y
CONFIG_USB_U_SERIAL=y
CONFIG_USB_U_ETHER=y
CONFIG_USB_F_ECM=y
CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS=y
